Battlemage resonance joins ordinary weapon attacks to a prepared barrage.

A wielded FOCUS may prepare a known barrage page even while it is still Copied,
and pays zero SP for its automatic casts. A worn AURA adds another cadence and
power improvement. Wearing both completes resonance. Investiture may supply
one missing half temporarily, but cannot create both halves by itself.

Mana Shard, Missile, Fireball, Icestorm, and Bolt can become barrages. Without
FOCUS they require Practiced mastery and spend SP. Their cadence improves with
mastery and Falx but ordinarily never becomes faster than once every two
combat rounds.
Concentration pauses the prepared page; silence and paralysis collapse it.

Beyond Arcane 15, a real wielded FOCUS changes the bargain. Barrage fires every
round and produces two to six complete barrages according to the weapon's WC
and item level. It does not copy the Mage's weapon-swing count. Instead, the
Mage gives up one swing below player level 50, then another at each 50-level
threshold, to a maximum of six at level 250. Investiture does not qualify.
The visual battlemage display condenses the FOCUS weapon's combined WC and item
level rating into a short Weave Power bar and shows how much remains before
the next barrage. Screen-reader output gives the same progress numerically.

Use "barrage <working>" to prepare a page, "barrage off" to release it, and
"battlemage" for the live FOCUS, AURA, cadence, SP, Overchannel, Grand
Revision, multibarrage exchange, and Recollection readout.
